    not_duplicate_of: []  # 482c
    pr_ref:  # 482c
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-02 merging PR #713. The merge SUCCEEDED; the step after it did not,\nand the failure is structural rather than transient.\n\nWHAT HAPPENS. merge-pr rebase-merges (which rewrites the SHA), then runs\n`git notes add` to attach the ORIGINAL commit body to the new commit -- the\nmechanism AGENTS.md documents under \"Git Notes\" for recovering bodies lost to a\nrebase. Pushing those notes trips the pre-push DCO hook:\n\n    BLOCKED: commit(s) missing a DCO Signed-off-by trailer\n      b33c08cb9f  Notes added by 'git notes add'\n      28894a1e8d  Notes added by 'git notes add'\n      ... ~40 more\n\nA notes commit's message is generated by git as \"Notes added by 'git notes add'\".\nIt can never carry a Signed-off-by trailer, so the hook can never pass on the\nnotes ref. This is not a flaky push -- it is unsatisfiable by construction.\n\nCONSEQUENCE. The documented body-preservation mechanism does not run on the\nrebase-merge path. The merge is unaffected and the body still exists in the PR\ndescription, so nothing is lost today; what is broken is a stated recovery route\nthat a future reader is told to rely on (\"Fetch with git fetch origin\nrefs/notes/*:refs/notes/*\"). AGENTS.md presents it as working.\n\nNOT SIZED, and worth sizing before fixing: the ~40 blocked notes commits suggest\nthis has been failing for a while rather than starting today, so the notes ref\non origin is probably well behind. Check how many merged commits actually carry\na note before deciding whether to backfill.\n\nFIX SHAPE, not chosen. The pre-push hook is a GOVERNANCE file (.githooks/**), so\nwhichever option is taken needs human approval and must not be self-merged.\n  1. Exempt refs/notes/* in the DCO hook. Narrow and correct -- DCO is a claim\n     about authorship of CONTENT, and a notes commit contains none. Requires\n     care that the exemption keys on the REF being pushed, not on the message.\n  2. Have merge-pr push notes with --no-verify. Smaller blast radius but it\n     teaches the reflex the hook exists to prevent.\n  3. Drop the notes mechanism and delete its AGENTS.md paragraph. Honest if the\n     bodies are not actually being consumed by anyone.\nOption 1 is the one that matches what the hook is for; option 3 is the one to\ntake if the sizing above shows the notes ref is already useless."  # 482c
    fields: {}  # 482c
