  message: "FOLDED into INV-nihaz and closed done — the work this item asked for shipped in PR #935 (merged 2026-09-12, dev dd50189f38).\n\nDUPLICATE, filed five days after the canonical row. INV-nihaz (2026-08-27) had already recorded the same mechanism, the same evidence and the same proposed two-line fix. Neither this item nor INV-fapub (2026-09-12, also folded) found it, because the three titles share almost no vocabulary — \"auto-pr git-note body preservation never reaches the remote\" / \"merge-pr git-notes body preservation is unsatisfiable\" / \"git notes have NEVER been pushed\". Three filings in sixteen days is a discoverability signal, not a diligence one; `tracker clusters` finds all three, a title search finds none.\n\nTHIS ITEMS OWN OPEN QUESTION IS ANSWERED. It said: \"NOT SIZED, and worth sizing before fixing: the ~40 blocked notes commits suggest this has been failing for a while ... Check how many merged commits actually carry a note before deciding whether to backfill.\" Sized: 727 notes, oldest 2026-01-22, and `git ls-remote origin refs/notes/*` was EMPTY — origin was not \"well behind\", it had nothing at all. INV-nihaz had already measured 565 of those five days before this item was written.\n\nCLOSED ON THIS ITEMS OWN FILED ROW. Its specific claim was about the merge-pr rebase path: \"merge-pr rebase-merges (which rewrites the SHA), then runs git notes add ... Pushing those notes trips the pre-push DCO hook\". That exact path was exercised by the merge of the fix itself, and now prints:\n\n    Attaching git note with original commit body...\n       Note attached to dd50189f388b3569bc34d603e8eef38b24cb3bc2 and pushed\n\nwhere it previously printed the BLOCKED banner. The notes ref on origin advanced with it. A fresh clone plus the AGENTS.md command now returns 728.\n\nWHAT FIXED IT: refs/notes/* exempted from the DCO block in .githooks/pre-push (a notes commit is written by git itself and can never carry a trailer), and scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh no longer swallows the push failure with 2>/dev/null || true — which is why this had failed 726 times in silence. A regression guard in .githooks/test_hooks.sh asserts the same unsigned commit blocked on refs/heads/t is allowed on refs/notes/commits; CI runs that file."  # a916
